Chapter: RocMutualEvenOdd
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_recursive_data_tests.zig,
 "inspect: mutually recursive functions" and "inspect: very deep recursion
 stack behavior":

     even = |n| if n == 0.I64 True else odd(n - 1.I64)
     odd  = |n| if n == 0.I64 False else even(n - 1.I64)
     main = (even(10.I64), odd(11.I64))            (True, True)

     depth = |n| if n == 0.I64 0.I64 else 1.I64 + depth(n - 1.I64)
     main = depth(512.I64)                          512

 Two definitions that each call the other, and one that recurses 512 deep
 without tail position. Booleans print as `true`/`false`; the tuple is two
 lines.

Section: Functions

  even : Integer -> Boolean
  even (n) = if n == 0 then True else odd (n - 1)

  odd : Integer -> Boolean
  odd (n) = if n == 0 then False else even (n - 1)

  depth : Integer -> Integer
  depth (n) = if n == 0 then 0 else 1 + depth (n - 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (if even 10 then "true" else "false")
   print-line-uni (if odd 11 then "true" else "false")
   print-line-uni (show (depth 512))
  end
